    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nWhat acid/base disorder does Acetazolamide cause?\n\nNormal anion gap metabolic acidosis\n\n(Remember, anion gap acidosis is due to production of volatile organic acids such as in diabetic ketoacidosis)\n\n[Image: 5242187d47e06f71c02a393953ec9710f1b5b8038780d9a09b0537a46c9d4201]\n\n2.1 - Acetazolamide, mannitol\n[Image: c346f1e1d5cb39cc059e5bd608d36a8812b1c3b530d0e01775017287fe4fe311]\n\n[Image: 61f8a0910486f3c71a4efb2db6dbb10d3bbc0bb7fb66229bb099924aa115e650]\n\n[Image: b76e775466426f4d4e1061c1f6bca824ec6b4d679966f6f7153af8a9243e768b]",
